WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.930 --> 00:00:03.763
- What?

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.370
Whose is that?

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.203
- Yours?

00:00:07.203 --> 00:00:11.280
- No, no, no, no, no, no, no,
no, no, no, no, no, no, no.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.113
Can I sit in it?

00:00:12.113 --> 00:00:12.946
No.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.313
For real?
- For real.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:20.107
I've never seen you cry like this.

00:00:20.107 --> 00:00:22.150
I'm here with Justin Bieber
today and today we're gonna see

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.160
what do people think about Justin Bieber?

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.260
- Oh my God, love him, but
Yummy is just like, not it.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.810
It's not that good.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.355
- It's not it!
- Oh my God!

00:00:29.355 --> 00:00:31.140
- It's not it?
- Oh my God!

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.665
- Here's 25 grand.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.498
- Oh!
- Oh!

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:36.958
- What?
- What?

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.041
(laughs)

00:00:40.043 --> 00:00:40.876
- David!

00:00:40.876 --> 00:00:42.890
- [David] My hands shaking, take it quick.

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.560
- Oh my God.
(audience applauds)

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:48.270
- To say our first guest is
a social media sensation,

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.900
well, that really just doesn't cut it.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.450
I'm actually really excited
about this interview

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.440
and I take it seriously because
David Dobrik is someone who,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.840
I feel, is a very unique and
important person in this world.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.650
He is someone who has a very loud voice

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:10.500
and a very big platform.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.310
And I'm really excited
to talk to him because

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:20.210
what he does in this world is meaningful.

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.000
And as someone who

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.550
loves joy

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.400
and silliness

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.900
and all of those things, the
other side of me is someone who

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.940
really cares about taking care of people

00:01:37.098 --> 00:01:40.510
and showing the
possibilities in the world.

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:44.990
And so when I think of David
Dobrik, I get really excited

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:47.590
because it isn't talk.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.370
It's all really happening in his world

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:51.870
and we're all watching it.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:56.573
So without further ado, ladies
and gentlemen, David Dobrik.

00:01:56.573 --> 00:01:58.261
(audience applauds)

00:01:58.261 --> 00:01:59.850
Hi.
- Hi.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.430
- How are you?
- How are you?

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.263
That was brutally nice.

00:02:05.243 --> 00:02:07.571
It seems like we paid
you off to say all that.

00:02:07.571 --> 00:02:08.404
That was like a paragraph.

00:02:08.404 --> 00:02:10.150
Usually I get here's
YouTuber, David Dobrik,

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.980
but that was awesome, thank you.

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:13.320
- No, no no.

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.320
You are anything but just a YouTuber.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.253
You are someone who,

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:21.340
first of all, your numbers.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.620
I mean eight billion views and,

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.620
you know, 20 million followers
is obviously so impressive.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:33.160
You know, I think back to
like Candid Camera and I think

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:37.160
about the history of the
medium of how you reach people

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.100
while being authentically who you are.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.160
Was there always a time
where you thought you wanted

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.910
to have this be this,
sort of like, feel good,

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:50.910
philanthropic, like surprise
people, pay mortgages,

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:52.840
like donate cars.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:57.840
When did you sort of think like
Oprah and Jackass would bake

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.370
a really potent combination
with a dash of brunt?

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:01.310
- That's funny.

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.143
- When did I first?

00:03:02.143 --> 00:03:03.320
I don't know, I was a big fan growing up.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.860
I was a big fan of
military surprise videos.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:08.230
Like I loved when soldiers
would come home from like

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.900
these long tours and they'd
surprise their families,

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:13.160
and I was like, I'm such
a sucker for reactions.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:15.530
Like whether someone's
reacting like they're terrified

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:18.400
or they're scared or they're super happy.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.020
Like I love it all.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.070
So when I got the chance
to surprise people

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.850
in a positive way rather
than like scare 'em

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.130
with like a spider or some
kind of an animal, that's what,

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.540
like, I wanted to lean towards.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.040
It's the most selfish
feeling to surprise others

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:33.930
with people, because like
the joy you get from them

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:38.360
being happy, is just like
it pays it back tenfold.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.300
Like it's the best.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.560
- And I think some people,
unfortunately, have a little bit

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:44.790
of a gotcha.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.710
I'm not a big fan of that.

00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:50.600
And when I watch your stuff,
there is such a goodness there.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.940
There is,
- Thanks

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.030
- there is this sweetness, this kindness,

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.880
this joy where you do
really get off at watching

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.600
people's reactions,
but it's based in good.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:01.710
- I always say that, like
the moments that you've seen

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:04.090
my videos are very much the real moments

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.740
that I'm experiencing in real life too.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.130
And that's why I like
making videos on YouTube

00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.920
is because it's such an intimate
thing and you can have such

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.070
an intimate interaction with
strangers and you can have like

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.000
that actual moment like when you're like,

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:19.150
there was a time we
surprised this DACA girl.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.820
I think it was with like
$25,000, I'm not sure.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:24.390
But like, it was just me
and her and her friends

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:26.300
sitting in, like, in her Jeep.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.800
And like, it feels all so real.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.330
And like being able to capture that moment

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.497
and having that forever is like the best.

00:04:33.497 --> 00:04:34.950
- And you are DACA.

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.870
You are a dreamer.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.073
- Right, yeah.

00:04:38.073 --> 00:04:41.970
- So is that personal in that moment?

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:46.070
- Yeah, it was really
funny 'cause I was in Texas

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.920
and this kid walks up to me and he goes,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.680
my girlfriend's DACA, just like you.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.000
I am too.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.160
She works two jobs.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:52.993
She has a kid.

00:04:52.993 --> 00:04:54.500
She's 19 years old.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.210
And then we went to go meet
up with her and her two

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.089
other friends were there,
and they were also all DACA.

00:05:00.089 --> 00:05:02.070
So it was like four or five
of us sitting in this car.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.070
And it was like so cool
because it was just a car full

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:07.320
of these illegals, including me. (laughs)

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.900
And we're just like
laughing and like, you know,

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.120
making light of our situation.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.000
And that was like the coolest
thing, like to to be able

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.820
to share a moment with
people like that, was like

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:17.920
really, really awesome.

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:21.930
- Something that I really
appreciated, and you just seem

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:25.760
so genuine to me and not
ego-driven and so much more

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:30.280
joy-driven, but when you
stopped doing your videos,

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.180
was there sort of a, I
need to just stop a moment.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.513
I don't know, what was it for you?

00:05:37.355 --> 00:05:41.150
- I think there's also this
thing with specifically people

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.750
in social media is it moves so quickly

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.930
and you're your own boss, so
you're pumping out content

00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.400
like as fast as you can.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:50.120
And I think it's a
really easy to get like,

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.290
so like infatuated with like
the instant gratification of it

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.840
and like, how quickly you can
make stuff and you just get

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:02.350
like addicted to like making
videos and making content.

00:06:02.350 --> 00:06:05.060
And I remember when I stopped,
it was like very much like

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.100
I was like entering civilization again.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.561
It was, I don't know how to explain it.

00:06:09.561 --> 00:06:11.130
It sounds so bizarre, but
it was like, I wasn't there.

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.940
And I was like never present for like

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.210
the last three, four years.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.410
I was just like in
this, like, in this zone

00:06:16.410 --> 00:06:18.640
of go, go go, and I know
it sounds ridiculous.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.890
And I know people are at home
like, he makes YouTube videos.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:21.760
Why is that?

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.090
But, that's what it felt like.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:27.479
- That's the thing, you don't
just make YouTube videos.

00:06:27.479 --> 00:06:28.510
- I appreciate that.
- And I think

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:31.510
that, I think you have a
big civil responsibility

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:34.550
on your hands because so
many people are watching you.

00:06:34.550 --> 00:06:39.090
And when you take a pause, I
think you are saying it is okay

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:42.630
for all of us to take off the helmet,

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.680
- Aw, thanks.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.060
- and stop for a minute.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.810
- It's really important
just to hit refresh

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:49.501
on the whole thing and just
take a moment and be like,

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.299
okay, this is what I was doing.

00:06:51.299 --> 00:06:52.539
This is what I need to change.

00:06:52.539 --> 00:06:53.820
And like you know, let me
get back to being a human

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:55.319
for a little bit.

00:06:55.319 --> 00:06:59.420
- You're very enthusiastic and
like charming and excitable

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:00.380
and all of those things.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.210
And believe me, I've been
thinking about this lately

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:03.960
because I have my dark moments.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.260
Do you have dark moments?

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:06.093
'Cause you're so

00:07:06.093 --> 00:07:07.622
excitable out there.
- 100 %.

00:07:07.622 --> 00:07:10.630
Like when the cameras are off,
I am a little dark and like,

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.620
I am hard on myself and
I'm not Miss Mary Sunshine.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.124
Like when the cameras go off,

00:07:15.124 --> 00:07:17.970
are you intense about your work?

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.450
Like, do you have a different
personality that comes up

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.333
a little bit?

00:07:22.345 --> 00:07:25.430
- I'm so, so hard on myself.

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:29.012
Yeah, but yeah, I think
that comes with anybody

00:07:29.012 --> 00:07:31.280
that wants, you know,
that is an entertainer.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.680
I think there are definitely dark moments,

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.352
but those aren't the moments
that you want other people

00:07:35.352 --> 00:07:36.550
to see for, you know, a number of reasons.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.950
But that doesn't take
away the authenticity

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:41.880
of the real moments that
you're actually drawing.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.571
It's not like, you know,
it's not like we come on here

00:07:44.571 --> 00:07:46.390
and we like put on this like
fake front where we're like,

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.190
we're happy, but really
behind closed doors

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:49.140
where we're miserable.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:51.790
I still think that I'm, you
know, for the most part,

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.780
a super, super happy person,
but there are definitely

00:07:53.780 --> 00:07:55.460
moments where I'm like, ah,

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.180
nothing's going my way right now.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.100
- So we're both crazy, but
we're both really happy.

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.150
And we both really care about what we do.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:06.910
I like that you're
hitting so many cylinders.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:07.923
You have a perfume.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:11.030
- Yeah, I have a perfume.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:13.400
I honestly, if I'm
being completely honest,

00:08:13.400 --> 00:08:15.240
why I did the perfume, other
than the fact that I like

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.880
really, really love it, I've
just been such a big fan

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:20.620
of perfume commercials and
commercials in general.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.480
And quite specifically,
there's a Natalie Portman

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.800
Dior commercial,
- Of course.

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:26.296
- that I'm like obsessed with.

00:08:26.296 --> 00:08:27.392
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:27.392 --> 00:08:28.580
I love Natalie Portman to death.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:31.640
So I'm always wanting to make
like a commercial on my own.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:34.350
So I got to make a little
commercial for my perfume,

00:08:34.350 --> 00:08:36.480
which I was really excited about.

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.590
And I'm just like a big fan of the scent.

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:42.950
- By the way, I am so excited for Dispo.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:44.040
Are you kidding?

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.000
That is
- A what?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.890
- going to be huge.

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:48.630
- Oh thanks, that means a lot.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.230
So now we're doing this Dispo
thing and it's slowly going

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.248
to turn into, sort of like
a social media where you can

00:08:55.248 --> 00:08:59.730
share those pictures with
other people that I used to go

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.580
to like some parties at my
friend's house and they would

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.770
put disposable cameras
all around the house.

00:09:03.770 --> 00:09:05.380
And instead of everyone
Instagramming all night

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:07.560
and waiting to get the
right shot and being like,

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.910
wait, wait, move here, move here,

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:12.480
they would just take
quick disposable pictures

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:14.500
and it literally never ruined a moment.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.333
Like, I don't know.

00:09:15.333 --> 00:09:17.090
I'm really excited for
that to make it work.

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:17.980
- You are just amazing.

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:20.750
I was so excited to talk to you,

00:09:20.750 --> 00:09:22.080
really and truly.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.580
I marvel at what you do.
- I was so excited

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.270
to talk to you.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.560
I really appreciate all
those words and I don't know.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.190
I'm sure you know by now,
but I'm the biggest fan

00:09:32.190 --> 00:09:33.650
of 50 First Dates.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:36.710
- I love that, but your friend,
Jason, doesn't agree, right?

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:37.543
- No, no.

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:40.000
So I was tryin' to tell him,
I was like 50 First Dates

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.780
is in the top 10 best movies of all time.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:45.921
And he just didn't understand it. (laughs)

00:09:45.921 --> 00:09:47.223
(audience laughs)

00:09:47.223 --> 00:09:48.850
Yeah.

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.510
- Well, actually, we're
gonna be right back

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:54.890
with a surprise for Jason, right?

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:55.723
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:55.723 --> 00:09:57.820
We have Jason on Zoom
and I'm gonna get him

00:09:57.820 --> 00:10:01.499
to talk a little crap
about 50 First Dates,

00:10:01.499 --> 00:10:04.310
and then you can appear
and set him straight.

00:10:04.310 --> 00:10:05.910
- I will see you in two minutes.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.286
We'll be right back.

00:10:08.286 --> 00:10:13.286
(audience applauds)
(upbeat music)

